       The  start  and  end  time of a lease are recorded using the ssttaarrttss and
       eennddss statements.   The ttssttpp statement is present if the failover proto‐
       col is being used, and indicates what time the peer has been  told  the
       lease  expires.    The  ttssffpp  statement is also present if the failover
       protocol is being used, and indicates the lease expiry  time  that  the
       peer  has  acknowledged.   The  aattssffpp statement is the actual time sent
       from the failover partner.  The cclltttt statement  is  the  client’s  last
       transaction time.

       See the description of dates in the section on common structures.

